  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.67:\n\t\t- Changed: rate-limit backoff is now logged at Information, and at Warning once the cumulative\n\t\t  wait for a request exceeds a full MaximumBackOffSeconds. Four of the five backoff sites logged\n\t\t  at Debug, so a client running at the default Information level saw nothing at all while the\n\t\t  429 loop waited - and that wait is unbounded in aggregate and silent by every other measure:\n\t\t  no CPU, no open socket, no exception. Telling a polite backoff from a hung call previously\n\t\t  meant thread dumps and socket sampling. The message now also carries the attempt number and\n\t\t  the total waited so far, not just the current delay, because the tenth five-minute wait reads\n\t\t  very differently from the first and only the client knows which it is.\n\t\t- Unchanged, deliberately: the 429 retry loop is still unbounded. Waiting as long as the portal\n\t\t  asks is defensible, and bounding it is a policy decision for callers rather than for this\n\t\t  client. The six Service Unavailable retry sites also remain at Debug, since those are bounded\n\t\t  by AttemptCount and so cannot wait indefinitely.",
